 ## Layout
 
-The creator runs the full width of the screen with 40px side margins on desktop: wordmark, a four-step tab bar spanning the width, then one parchment panel. Inside panels, content splits into two or three equal columns (abilities, drive columns) with 16px to 24px gaps, and collapses to one column on phones. Every control in the creator is 44px on a touch screen, a phone's too (playtest, 2026-10-10): the step tabs, the fields and buttons (the Join a Campaign dialog's too, a form the roster book shares), and in the action ratings (step 3) the gild star (its hit area clear of the action's name), the free-raise chips and the steppers. On a tablet the action ratings keep the three drives one under another below xl, so each action's row has room for them on one line; on a phone the row keeps its 44px controls by putting the rating pips under the action's name. On every touch screen, a phone's too, each action has the desk's printed "i" (`shared/ActionInfo.jsx`) for what it does, which a mouse reads on hover (iPad pass, 2026-10-05).
+The creator runs the full width of the screen with 40px side margins on desktop: wordmark, a four-step tab bar spanning the width, then one parchment panel. Inside panels, content splits into two or three equal columns (abilities, drive columns) with 16px to 24px gaps, and collapses to one column on phones. Every control in the creator is 44px on a touch screen, a phone's too (playtest, 2026-10-10): the step tabs, the fields and buttons (the Join a Campaign dialog's too, a form the roster book shares), and in the action ratings (step 3) the gild star (its hit area clear of the action's name), the free-raise chips and the steppers. On a tablet the action ratings keep the three drives one under another below xl, so each action's row has room for them on one line; on a phone the row keeps its 44px controls by putting the rating pips under the action's name, and under about 356px, where the steppers no longer fit beside the name, "i" and star, they wrap to a line of their own so nothing is wider than the screen down to 320px (#26). On every touch screen, a phone's too, each action has the desk's printed "i" (`shared/ActionInfo.jsx`) for what it does, which a mouse reads on hover (iPad pass, 2026-10-05).
 
 The GM desk is a three-column workspace under the Lightkeeper's Desk bar, which carries its tabs as the player's member ID strip does (issue #66.3): on the Roster a left rail with the pinned dispatch, a center work surface, and a right rail with the dice tray, activity log and pass-notes. The chapter hub is a free composition of overlapping objects (tomes, newspaper, pamphlets) on a dark desk.
 
